# Back-end settings. Every setting is optional; each comment says what applies
# while its line stays commented out, and the value shown is an example.
# To change a setting, copy this file to back-end/.env
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env
# and uncomment the line. A variable already set in the environment wins over
# this file. Restart the back end after editing .env.

# The agent that runs turns. Supported: claude, scripted. Default: claude.
# Use scripted for development and tests — it replays fixed turns with no AI
# calls. Include a marker in the instructor message to choose a scenario:
#   (no marker) or [ok]  — valid SCORM package, QA passes
#   [qa-fail]            — package the QA gate rejects
#   [follow-up]          — version 2 with additional questions
#   [signed-out]         — agent_signed_out error
#   [busy]               — agent_busy error
#   [long-step]          — a slow turn (~5 s)
#   [cancelled]          — turn is cancelled mid-run
# AGENT_DRIVER=claude

# The model the agent uses. Default: the agent's default for the signed-in account.
# AGENT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# How much reasoning effort the agent spends: low, medium, high, xhigh, or max.
# Default: the agent's default.
# AGENT_EFFORT=high

# The most model calls one request may make, a whole number of 1 or more.
# Default: 60, over twice the largest real request (27 steps).
# AGENT_MAX_STEPS=40

# The most one request may spend, in US dollars. Default: 10, about three times
# the largest real request ($3.25). Claude counts cost at API prices, even on a
# subscription.
# AGENT_MAX_BUDGET_USD=5

# The port the back end listens on at 127.0.0.1, a whole number from 1 to 65535.
# Default: 3000. When you change it, point the front end at it with
# API_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:<port>.
# PORT=4000

# Where the database, workspaces, and builds are stored. A relative path is
# resolved against back-end/. Default: %LOCALAPPDATA%\CDK on Windows, ~/.cdk elsewhere.
# DATA_DIR=D:\CDK

# The origin the app is opened at, and the only one allowed to frame build
# previews. Default: http://127.0.0.1:5173, the Vite dev server. Previews are
# served on http://preview.localhost:<PORT>.
# APP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:3000

# A secret the packaged app creates on each launch and passes to its window.
# When set, every API request must carry it in the X-CDK-Token header. Leave
# unset during development — origin checking alone is enough.
# LAUNCH_TOKEN=

# The built front end to serve at / on the back end's own origin, as the desktop
# app does. Default: unset, so only the API and previews are served. Set
# APP_ORIGIN to http://127.0.0.1:<PORT> with it. A relative path is resolved
# against back-end/.
# APP_DIR=../front-end/dist

# Read by the Claude CLI, not by the back end. Default: the Claude sign-in on
# this machine. The agent receives only its sign-in and the variables it needs
# to run; no other setting here reaches it.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=your-api-key
